[{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.036795376,"data":"# Kaggle kernel agent guide\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.036865703,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.036871913,"data":"This file travels inside every kernel that `scripts/kaggle_run.py` pushes\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.036876111,"data":"and is printed at the top of its log. The repository's root AGENTS.md owns\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.036879977,"data":"every rule; this guide states what a Kaggle kernel is for, what it runs on,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.036884066,"data":"and what it must prove before its output counts.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.036893745,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.036896405,"data":"## What runs where\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.036898843,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.036901319,"data":"| Substrate | Runs | Never runs |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.036903801,"data":"| --- | --- | --- |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.036906386,"data":"| Kaggle GPU kernel (Aer on GPU) | every simulation of 14 qubits or fewer: noise simulations under a retained calibration export, design power analyses, parameter sweeps | IBM jobs; anything needing an IBM credential |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.036924058,"data":"| Kaggle CPU in the same kernel | transpilation, package builds, the hypercomplex table extraction | |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.036941471,"data":"| Kaggle TPU (`TpuV5E8`, `TpuV6E8`) | JAX code only; Aer has no TPU backend. Batch pushes requesting either ID ran on 4-core CPU machines without libtpu, so this account reaches no TPU through the CLI | Qiskit or Aer |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.036946925,"data":"| Kaggle Gemma models (attached through `model_sources`) | text tasks on request | evidence: a language-model answer supports no physical or mathematical claim |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.036951631,"data":"| IBM Heron (ibm_fez, ibm_kingston, ibm_marrakesh) | 15 or more qubits, or a question about a named device qubit, only after the owner approves a written case | simulations |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.036956681,"data":"| GitHub Actions CPU | the CPU replay gate that re-derives a reduced case of each Kaggle result | GPU work |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.036961358,"data":"| Build host (Arch, RTX 4070 Ti 12 GB; guide in the untracked `docs/local/`) | development, dry runs, calibration exports, CPU replays, the Arch-packaged hypercomplex stack and SageMath | runs the routing rule sends to Kaggle |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.036965803,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.036969417,"data":"## Every kernel's phases\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.036973083,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.036976714,"data":"`kaggle_kernel/kernel_main.py` writes one JSON file per phase into\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.036980547,"data":"`/kaggle/working/output`:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.036984375,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.036987882,"data":"1. `environment.json`: Python and package versions, CPU model and cores,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.036991665,"data":"   RAM, working disk, every GPU (name, memory, driver, compute capability),\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.036995503,"data":"   CUDA driver version, TPU devices, Aer devices and attached models.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.036999325,"data":"2. `hypercomplex.json`: the hypercomplex stack. The kernel fetches the eight\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.037021996,"data":"   pinned archives (sha256-checked), installs them through the PKGBUILD\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.037037178,"data":"   recipes in `scripts/algebra_package_tables.py`, runs `--extract`, and\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.03704236,"data":"   stops with exit code 3 unless the regenerated\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.037047091,"data":"   `docs/evidence/algebra_packages/tables.json` equals the retained bytes.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.037052186,"data":"   The build host passes the same test against its Arch packages, so a run\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.037066802,"data":"   that reaches its entry used the same algebra code as the host.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.03707092,"data":"3. `capacity.json` (smoke kernels): the widest GHZ circuit each Aer method\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.037074899,"data":"   runs on the GPU.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.037078716,"data":"4. The entry's stdout, stderr, exit code and changed files.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.037082631,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.0370863,"data":"## Package stack\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.037090038,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.037093678,"data":"| Package | Pin | Kernel source |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.037097568,"data":"| --- | --- | --- |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.037101292,"data":"| qiskit | 2.5.2 | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.037105141,"data":"| qiskit-aer-gpu-cu11 | 0.17.2 (the CUDA 12 `qiskit-aer-gpu` stops at 0.15.1 and has no Python 3.13 wheel) | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.037109302,"data":"| hypercomplex, hypercomplex-engine, hypercomplex-algebra, Cayley-Calculator, octonion, mathdunders | 0.3.4, 0.5.0, 0.2.0.2, 1.3.1, 0.1.0, 0.4.2 | PyPI sdist, sha256-pinned |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.037115754,"data":"| cayley-dickson, SplitOct | commits abf96e7, e29e72f | GitHub archive, sha256-pinned, PKGBUILD recipe |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.037124052,"data":"| numpy-quaternion | 2024.0.13 | PyPI (Cayley-Calculator runtime) |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.037152602,"data":"| numpy, scipy, sympy, pandas, torch | Kaggle image versions, recorded per run | Kaggle image |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.037157271,"data":"| SageMath | 10.10 | build host only; a computation that needs Sage stays there |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.037161605,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.0371659,"data":"## Rules\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.037170053,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.037173545,"data":"- A kernel is private, has GPU and internet enabled, and holds no IBM\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.037177321,"data":"  credential. Noise comes from a retained\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.037181028,"data":"  `gororoba_quantum/calibration_snapshot.py` export.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.037184689,"data":"- The entry reads `GOROROBA_AER_DEVICE` and selects the GPU through it.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.037188388,"data":"- An output is a numerical simulation. It enters\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.037192091,"data":"  `docs/state/research_state.json` only after a CPU replay gate re-derives\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.03719582,"data":"  a reduced case.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.037199464,"data":"- The push selects hardware with `--accelerator`; `environment.json`\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.037203234,"data":"  records what actually ran.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.03720691,"data":"- Measured limits of each machine shape, the qubit size guide and the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.037214756,"data":"  captured Kaggle documentation are in `docs/notes/kaggle/`.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":36.037218536,"data":"\n"}
